 ongoing efforts to best use our resources and infrastructure. For more information, see Note 4—Restructuring Charges to our Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements.","section":"Item 2. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations.","block":278,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001166003-26-000074","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001166003","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1166003/000116600326000074/xpo-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/44048dc885dbc586046a68362a47bf3b90c3ec6697fdb2849080034d52b5ec5a.bin","sha256":"44048dc885dbc586046a68362a47bf3b90c3ec6697fdb2849080034d52b5ec5a"}},{"id":"d85592602719695fd3e23edbd5776f20e79b330212ff20ee662c2d70c081807f","quote":"Our chief operating decision maker (“CODM”) regularly reviews financial information at the operating segment level to allocate resources to the segments and to assess their performance. For our North American LTL and European Transportation segments, our CODM evaluates segment profit (loss) based on adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization (“adjusted EBITDA”), which we define as income before debt extinguishment loss, interest expense, income tax provision, depreciation and amortization expense, legal matters, transaction and integration costs, restructuring costs and other adjustments. Segment adjusted EBITDA includes an allocation of corporate costs. See Note 2—Segment Reporting to our Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements for further information and a reconciliation of adjusted EBITDA to consolidated net income.","context":"Segment Financial Results","section":"Item 2. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations.","block":286,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","sou